body:
This adds named parameters when instanciating `instantsearch`, instead of having fixed arguments:

``` javascript
var search = instantsearch({
  applicationID: 'latency',
  searchAPIKey: '6be0576ff61c053d5f9a3225e2a90f76',
  indexName: 'instant_search'
});
```

This is needed for #77. I used `searchAPIKey` instead of `apiKey` to be explicit that this plugin is used for search only (we often have people on support using the wrong key). Better be explicit.

comments.body:
> Do we really need to introduce named parameters here? I

@redox: https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/issues/77#issuecomment-139495739

We were going to have:

``` js
var search = instantsearch('latency', '6be0576ff61c053d5f9a3225e2a90f76', 'instant_search', {
  numberLocale: 'fr_FR'
}, {searchParameters});
```

So you do not have to remember param names but you have to remember param order for 5 params.
